Want me to add a tiny debounce so rapid multi-cell pastes only trigger one validation per section within ~300ms?

Yes—here’s a lightweight debounce so rapid multi-cell pastes only trigger one validation per section (~300 ms). It uses CacheService to coalesce bursts and Utilities.sleep to wait briefly before validating.

Drop-in replacement for onEdit plus a small helper:

function onEdit(e) {
  try {
    const sh = e.range.getSheet();
    const col = e.range.getColumn();
    const row = e.range.getRow();
    if (col !== 3) return; // only watch column C

    if (row >= 3 && row <= 10) {
      debounceAndValidateSection_(sh, 'Option A', 3, 10, 'A');
    } else if (row >= 18 && row <= 25) {
      debounceAndValidateSection_(sh, 'Option B', 18, 25, 'B');
    }
  } catch (_) {
    // swallow errors in simple trigger
  }
}

// Debounce per section (~300 ms); coalesces rapid edits/pastes
function debounceAndValidateSection_(sh, name, start, end, keySuffix) {
  const cache = CacheService.getDocumentCache();
  const key = 'ev_debounce_' + keySuffix;
  const hit = cache.get(key);
  if (hit) return; // another event already scheduled within the window

  // Set a short-lived flag (0.5s) to absorb further rapid edits
  cache.put(key, '1', 1); // seconds (min granularity is 1s)

  // Small delay to let batch pastes settle, then validate once
  Utilities.sleep(300);
  validateSectionPartial(sh, name, start, end);
  SpreadsheetApp.getActive().toast(name + ' validated', 'EV Tools', 3);
}

Notes
- CacheService min TTL is 1 second; that’s fine for a ~300 ms debounce/coalescing window.
- Utilities.sleep(300) waits briefly so a multi-cell paste settles before validation.
- No other changes needed; your validateSectionPartial stays the same.

